This is a small example how to use a AHT20 Temperature and Humidity sensor with Oxocard Connect and breadbard card.
Look at the image how to wire the sensor on the breadboard.
The code show also how to connect to a i2c device without having the library for easy use. The sensor have no register, so the first byte of a command is put 
into the register parameter (this took some days to find this simple workarround)

Press the down button to exist the program.

The sensor itsself also contain a bmp280 sensor for pressure and additionaal temperature. See the BMP280 example how to read data from this sensor.
